{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest","id":1082773,"title":"[Homebrew Legacy] The Thread-Cutters (To the Strongest)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-23T14:40:43-07:00","id":1082773,"title":"[Homebrew Legacy] The Thread-Cutters (To the Strongest)","content":"So, I came up with this write-up for the Thread-Cutter Legacy specifically for the To the Strongest era, but I think it could mostly function for the modern day as well.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B_p2wvB4Nb9JbWZ3cV9fa09pcEk\" target=\"_blank\">Write-Up Here</a><br /> <br /> <br /> This is my first attempt at homebrewing a Legacy (or honestly homebrewing anything Mage related), so comments are welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-24-2017, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T15:44:25-07:00","id":1082799,"title":"","content":"Oaths Fulfilled will only last a few seconds without Reach assigned to Advanced Duration, and since it monitors if a person is or isn't doing something that the Mage dictates it may not be a good indicator of if a person is or isn't fulfilling their Dharma as written.<br /> <br /> For the Death 2 Optional it ought to succeed automatically against any non-supernatural person, entities who might be able to examine them via supernatural means to pierce their disguise would engage them in a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> The 3rd attainment will only be useful against supernatural efforts, which is maybe a bit narrow for an attainment but mechanically it's fine. I'd allow them to be able to use it on themselves as well giving them a pretty good defense in those areas.<br /> <br /> The 5th attainment is pretty badass. Good work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T16:01:10-07:00","id":1082806,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1059965#post1059965\">Here</a> is another Thread-Cutter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T21:43:09-07:00","id":1082899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082799#post1082799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oaths Fulfilled will only last a few seconds without Reach assigned to Advanced Duration, and since it monitors if a person is or isn't doing something that the Mage dictates it may not be a good indicator of if a person is or isn't fulfilling their Dharma as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I was wondering how exactly to go about it since First Attainments are a little short on the Reach. Ended up changing it to a scene of Meditation to open one's Third Eye to the Wheel for the Duration. Since with even the basic Fate 2 needed to join the Legacy this means the power lasts the whole day (unless I'm mistaken) I figure the Mage can spend a scene at the beginning of the day activating this power and have it for the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082799#post1082799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Death 2 Optional it ought to succeed automatically against any non-supernatural person, entities who might be able to examine them via supernatural means to pierce their disguise would engage them in a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082799#post1082799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 3rd attainment will only be useful against supernatural efforts, which is maybe a bit narrow for an attainment but mechanically it's fine. I'd allow them to be able to use it on themselves as well giving them a pretty good defense in those areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering this...the mythos I developed for this legacy kind of forbids them from materially benefiting from their Attainments, hence why the Second and Fourth ones explicitly state that you can't use them on yourself. On the other hand, Warding Gesture and Soul Armour aren't exactly material benefits, I ended up letting them use it as a way to represent the resilience of their Soul through connection to the Wheel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082799#post1082799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 5th attainment is pretty badass. Good work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T22:05:24-07:00","id":1082902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082806#post1082806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1059965#post1059965\">Here</a> is another Thread-Cutter</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the link <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's an interesting take on the Legacy as well, though I was trying to do with just the First Attainment what 21C Hermit designed the first two to do, and the goading part of the Fourth Attainment goes counter to the subtle mythos I was going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:11:20-07:00","id":1082923,"title":"","content":"We can always say that the two Legacy write-ups are two different branches, whose different interpretations of the Legacy's ethos lead to developing different sets of Attainments, since developing novel Attainments are a canon thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T03:37:22-07:00","id":1082956,"title":"","content":"So, the thing about the first attainment is that the spell it's modeled on is cast on another person and not the Mage themselves. However considering its limited application I'd set it up with a ritual activation that doesn't designate a subject of the attainment, later as he goes about his day he can touch a person and designate them the subject of the attainment and then it will monitor if they break the Dharma. You should keep an eye on what the Duration was after activating the attainment because the Duration will start its countdown from before you touch the subject, not after. So for instance your arcana allow you to maintain a Duration of 24 hours (Fate 2 Advanced Duration Reach) activate the attainment, three hours later you give the attainment it's subject by touching them, so the attainment will monitor them for 21 more hours. Then after delivering a touch and giving the attainment a subject you can activate the attainment via ritual and prepare it for another subject. As that Advanced Duration increases it'll get a lot less book-keepy since your Duration will be weeks and years. It'll be like building a tracking device from scratch, turning it on, and then sticking it on someone and you can keep doing it as many times to as many subjects as you want but you always have to take that hour to build the device from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:56:11-07:00","id":1083060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082956#post1082956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the thing about the first attainment is that the spell it's modeled on is cast on another person and not the Mage themselves. However considering its limited application I'd set it up with a ritual activation that doesn't designate a subject of the attainment, later as he goes about his day he can touch a person and designate them the subject of the attainment and then it will monitor if they break the Dharma. You should keep an eye on what the Duration was after activating the attainment because the Duration will start its countdown from before you touch the subject, not after. So for instance your arcana allow you to maintain a Duration of 24 hours (Fate 2 Advanced Duration Reach) activate the attainment, three hours later you give the attainment it's subject by touching them, so the attainment will monitor them for 21 more hours. Then after delivering a touch and giving the attainment a subject you can activate the attainment via ritual and prepare it for another subject. As that Advanced Duration increases it'll get a lot less book-keepy since your Duration will be weeks and years. It'll be like building a tracking device from scratch, turning it on, and then sticking it on someone and you can keep doing it as many times to as many subjects as you want but you always have to take that hour to build the device from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, going back and reading the Oaths Fulfilled and Interconnections Spells and thinking about what I really want from that First Attainment, I actually now think that just Interconnections is a better base spell to go off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This spell reveals the marks of Fate on people, places, and things the mage observes (up to one subject per turn). In addition to allowing the mage to detect any sympathetic connections between the subjects, the mage can also identify <b>those who<br /> have violated an oath or geas</b>, and the presence of spells with conditional Durations. </div> </div> </div>Basically I'm now considering taking a page out of 21c Hermit's page and making the Attainment into a version of Interconnections that <i>only</i> does the bolded part, only instead of Oaths or Geasa it tells you if the person being observed is upholding or has violated his Dharma. And, as I understand it, the subject of an Unveiling spell is the person being given the perception, not the thing being perceived, so subject as a consideration is no longer an issue. The Attainment still uses a scene long ritual and the Reach is spent on Advanced Duration meaning even a beginning Thread-Cutter (assuming he has Death 2) who starts the day with a ritual to open his inner eye now can tell the Dharmic status of anyone he meets for the rest of the day, and then follow up on any anomalies, instead of tagging people with homing signals.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:57:53-07:00","id":1083062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082773-homebrew-legacy-the-thread-cutters-to-the-strongest?p=1082923#post1082923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can always say that the two Legacy write-ups are two different branches, whose different interpretations of the Legacy's ethos lead to developing different sets of Attainments, since developing novel Attainments are a canon thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, totally...some of them are probably culture specific to different branches of the Legacy...I mean, turning into a gaunt emaciated mendicant might be useful in India, but I'm not sure it wouldn't attract way too much attention to be useful in downtown Dublin <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:33:50-07:00","id":1083079,"title":"","content":"It would work as an Instant Cast at that point and the short Duration would be less of an issue, still needs to be used on the subject though. A lot of Unveiling spells target a subject other than the caster, Mental Scan for instance. Notice how Interconnections is Withstood by Composure? It's cast on someone other than the Mage. Like I said though, using that instead for an immediate info download of whether or not someone has violated the Dharma should be workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}